IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hesa-help`

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth) -- indexed figures and limits computed from the formulas in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.formulas.md, beside hesa-help.l4 (unchanged, which takes the indexed HELP loan limit,
-- the indexed repayment thresholds and the reduced HELP debt indexation factor as inputs).
--
-- Formulas used:
--   * s 140-10(1A): HELP debt indexation factor = 1 + ([(A - 1) / 365] x [365 - B]), where A is the s 140-10(1)(b) factor and B
--     the days the Secretary determined under s 142-10(2) or 144-5(2); rounded to 3 places under s 140-10(1), (2);
--   * s 198-15(1): indexation factor = The index number for the December reference quarter / The index number for the December
--     base quarter, "to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more)" (s 198-15(2)); s 198-10: indexed
--     each 1 January by multiplying by the factor, not if the factor "is 1 or less", rounded "down to the nearest dollar";
--   * s 154-25(2): replacement amount = Indexable amount for the 2025-26 income year x (AWE for the indexation year / AWE for the
--     2025-26 income year), rounded down to the dollar (s 154-25(3)) -- for the minimum repayment income ($67,000) and the
--     s 154-20(2) upper threshold ($125,000);
--   * s 36-45: limit = Maximum student contribution amount for a place x The EFTSL value of the unit;
--   * s 128C-10(1)(b): maximum = The amount mentioned in paragraph (a) x The EFTSL value of the accelerator program course.
-- The CPI index numbers and AWE figures are the Australian Statistician's: inputs.
--
-- SEAT: the student or HELP debtor, as in hesa-help.l4. Edition: C2026C00297, as hesa-help.l4. BASELINE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Higher Education Support Act -- indexed figures and limits, computed`

§§ `s 140-10(1A) -- a reduced HELP debt indexation factor`

-- s 140-10(1)(a): where the Secretary has determined under s 142-10 or 144-5 that indexation is to be reduced (a very remote area
-- doctor or nurse, for example). Rounded to 3 places, the third raised if the fourth "would be a number greater than 4" (s
-- 140-10(2)).
@export What is my reduced HELP debt indexation factor, where the Secretary has reduced my indexation (s 140-10(1A))?
GIVEN `the ordinary factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The HELP debt indexation factor for 1 June under s 140-10(1)(b) (the lower of the CPI and WPI factors)
      `days determined` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the calendar year the Secretary determined for you under s 142-10(2) or 144-5(2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my reduced HELP debt indexation factor` IS
    FLOOR ((`unrounded` TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000
    WHERE
        `unrounded` MEANS 1 PLUS (((`the ordinary factor` MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 365) TIMES (365 MINUS `days determined`))

§§ `ss 198-10, 198-15 -- indexation of the HELP loan limit and the maximum contributions`

@export What is the Part 5-6 indexation factor for a 1 January (s 198-15)?
GIVEN `index number for the December reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter a year and a day before the 1 January
      `index number for the December base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter two years and a day before it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Part 5-6 indexation factor` IS
    FLOOR (((`index number for the December reference quarter` DIVIDED BY `index number for the December base quarter`) TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

@export What does an amount indexed under Part 5-6 become on 1 January (s 198-10)?
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount before the 1 January (the HELP loan limit, a maximum student contribution amount for a place, ...)
      `index number for the December reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter a year and a day before the 1 January
      `index number for the December base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter two years and a day before it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What does a Part 5-6 amount become on 1 January` IS
    IF `f` AT MOST 1 THEN `the amount` ELSE FLOOR (`the amount` TIMES `f`)
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `What is the Part 5-6 indexation factor` `index number for the December reference quarter` `index number for the December base quarter`

@desc The item at a position in a list of numbers (0 for the first), or NOTHING if the list is too short
GIVEN `xs` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The list
      `n` IS A NUMBER @desc The position, 0 for the first
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the HESA index number at` MEANS
    CONSIDER `xs`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `x` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN IF `n` AT MOST 0 THEN JUST `x` ELSE `the HESA index number at` `rest` (`n` MINUS 1)

-- From a figure known to be in force from 1 January of a start year, each later 1 January in turn. The December index numbers are
-- listed from the December quarter two years before the start year, one a year: 1 January of year Y uses the December quarters of
-- Y - 1 (item Y - start year + 1) and Y - 2 (item Y - start year).
@export What is an amount indexed under Part 5-6 in force from 1 January of a year, from a known figure (ss 198-10, 198-15)?
GIVEN `the known figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in force from 1 January of the start year
      `start year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year from whose 1 January the known figure was in force
      `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year asked about
      `december index numbers` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc CPI index numbers for December quarters, from two years before the start year, one a year in order
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `year` LESS THAN `start year` THEN NOTHING
           IF `year` EQUALS `start year` THEN JUST `the known figure`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January` `the known figure` `start year` (`year` MINUS 1) `december index numbers`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST `before` THEN
                   CONSIDER `the HESA index number at` `december index numbers` (`year` MINUS `start year` PLUS 1)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                   WHEN JUST `reference` THEN
                       CONSIDER `the HESA index number at` `december index numbers` (`year` MINUS `start year`)
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                       WHEN JUST `base` THEN JUST (`What does a Part 5-6 amount become on 1 January` `before` `reference` `base`)

-- The HELP balance (s 128-15) on an indexed limit. The s 128-20 figures ($106,319; $152,700) are taken as the start figures for
-- the year the caller names: whether the compiled figure was in force from 1 January of that year is the caller's statement.
@export How much can I still borrow, with the HELP loan limit indexed from the figure s 128-20 states (ss 128-15, 128-20, 198-10)?
GIVEN `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled in a course in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation
      `the year the stated limit applies from` IS A NUMBER @desc The year from whose 1 January the limit s 128-20 states was in force
      `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year asked about
      `december index numbers` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc CPI index numbers for December quarters, from two years before that start year
      `assistance previously payable` IS A NUMBER @desc HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP, VET FEE-HELP and VET student loan amounts previously payable for you, in dollars
      `amounts re-credited` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts previously re-credited to your HELP balance, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much can I still borrow on the indexed limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is the Part 5-6 amount in force from 1 January`
                 (`What is my HELP loan limit` `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation`)
                 `the year the stated limit applies from` `year` `december index numbers`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `limit` THEN JUST (max 0 (`limit` MINUS (`assistance previously payable` MINUS `amounts re-credited`)))

§§ `ss 154-10, 154-20, 154-25 -- the repayment thresholds from average weekly earnings`

-- s 154-25(2): from 2026-27, each indexable amount is the 2025-26 amount x (AWE for the indexation year / AWE for 2025-26), rounded
-- down to the dollar. 2025-26: the stated $67,000 and $125,000. Earlier years: the repealed text, not deposited: NOTHING.
@export What is my minimum repayment income, worked out from average weekly earnings (ss 154-10, 154-25)?
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year starts (2025 for 2025-26)
      `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the income year (s 154-25(2)), in dollars
      `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the 2025-26 income year, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my minimum repayment income from AWE` IS
    BRANCH IF `income year starting in` LESS THAN 2025 THEN NOTHING
           IF `income year starting in` EQUALS 2025 THEN JUST 67000
           OTHERWISE JUST (`What does an indexable amount become` 67000 `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`)

@export What is the s 154-20(2) upper repayment threshold, worked out from average weekly earnings (ss 154-20, 154-25)?
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year starts (2025 for 2025-26)
      `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the income year (s 154-25(2)), in dollars
      `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the 2025-26 income year, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the upper repayment threshold from AWE` IS
    BRANCH IF `income year starting in` LESS THAN 2025 THEN NOTHING
           IF `income year starting in` EQUALS 2025 THEN JUST 125000
           OTHERWISE JUST (`What does an indexable amount become` 125000 `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`)

-- s 154-1 and s 154-20 with the thresholds worked out: nothing if not liable (s 154-1), else the least of the marginal amount,
-- 10% of repayment income and the repayable debt.
@export How much compulsory HELP repayment must I make, with the thresholds worked out from average weekly earnings (ss 154-1, 154-20, 154-25)?
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year starts (2025 for 2025-26)
      `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the income year (s 154-25(2)), in dollars
      `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER @desc AWE for the 2025-26 income year, in dollars
      `repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `repayable debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your repayable debt for the income year (s 154-15), in dollars
      `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an accumulated HELP debt on the 1 June before your assessment
      `no Medicare levy payable under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you pay no Medicare levy under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986
      `Medicare levy reduced under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your Medicare levy is reduced under s 8
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much compulsory HELP repayment must I make from AWE` IS
    CONSIDER `What is my minimum repayment income from AWE` `income year starting in` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `minimum` THEN
        CONSIDER `What is the upper repayment threshold from AWE` `income year starting in` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `upper` THEN
            IF `Must I make a compulsory repayment` `repayment income` `minimum` `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June` `no Medicare levy payable under s 8` `Medicare levy reduced under s 8`
            THEN JUST (`How much is my compulsory repayment` `repayment income` `minimum` `upper` `repayable debt`)
            ELSE JUST 0

§§ `ss 36-45, 128C-10 -- the most I can be charged`

-- s 36-45: the provider's student contribution amount for the unit must not exceed (formula) the maximum student contribution
-- amount for a place x the EFTSL value of the unit.
@export What is the most my provider may charge me as the student contribution amount for a unit (s 36-45)?
GIVEN `maximum student contribution amount for a place` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum student contribution amount for a place in the unit (s 93-10, as indexed), in dollars
      `EFTSL value of the unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's EFTSL value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my provider may charge for the unit` IS
    `maximum student contribution amount for a place` TIMES `EFTSL value of the unit`

-- s 128C-10(1)(b): for an accelerator program course of less than one EFTSL, the maximum course fee is (formula) the amount in
-- paragraph (a) x the course's EFTSL value; (2): dollars and cents rounded "down to the nearest dollar". Paragraph (a) is the
-- s 93-10 item 4 maximum for Medicine, Dentistry or Veterinary Science (as indexed).
@export What is the most I can be charged for an accelerator program course of less than one EFTSL (s 128C-10(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the amount in paragraph (a)` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount s 128C-10(1)(a) sets for a course of one EFTSL, in dollars
      `EFTSL value of the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The course's EFTSL value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be charged for an accelerator program course` IS
    FLOOR (`the amount in paragraph (a)` TIMES `EFTSL value of the course`)
